cademy-id "q-18259" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-18259/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-18259"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42050/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "3e0b5e85-44cb-557e-9206-9a37087a8708" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42050/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "d29093a6-9bbf-5e1f-9b1c-b204bc15c666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42050/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "28353255-7392-53a2-adc7-d8a24ed1c5c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42050/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "c491227b-4068-593a-ba43-4a57916592b5" :ans