epiped is\n\n$$\nV=|2|=2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-42050/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42050"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "fecbdbfd-7093-5809-9a05-43b41ec72c61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" :answer/id #uuid "06c615b6-22b7-56af-a72a-dd2339cfde92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "22" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221/selection/990bd0b27231862ff8a458863a415b3ca1c1ea608954b3242d9a98208f25c769" :answer/id #uuid "8a9dbd75-1207-5c9d-b7af-52d043d2ba3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "59" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221/selection/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e" :answer/id #uuid "15db8fd3-a04e-5dbd-b62c-8c9c88d84d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "7ecf3894-0b3a-5cbc-a9fd-f9405c012274" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "00d97457-7080-5315-ab17-df1a145f1cc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40221/selection/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e" :answer-field/choices ["q-40221/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-40221/selection/12b48b00f9c1ff14570ca66bc629787a88856efba1cda24cfb28da58c148801a" "q-40221/selection/990bd0b27231862ff8a458863a415b3ca1c1ea608954b3242d9a98208f25c769" "q-40221/selection/e645b0f714e0f14adf4a4392c1fd41e203b4d4c946a42f546b48043b8700d60e" "q-40221/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40221" :question/id #uuid "d563b67f-cff3-5de6-b840-59edf3c18de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-40221" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-5,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,4⟩$ and $c=⟨1,1,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)-3(2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)+0 \\\\  & =25+6 \\\\  & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|31|=31.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40221/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40221"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" :answer/id #uuid "d689606a-b1d6-5a47-96a7-8235a9f0c345" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" :answer/id #uuid "c1f97eb6-6e15-5c61-a786-93ddc8911b49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "91517ee9-d156-547e-8050-cdec91a0f02e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "22e964b6-4cdd-56c8-b63d-95b29bec5809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "5ac9f39d-1e76-5ac0-ae9b-161f2e81b5cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a574109-36b8-5949-9b70-4eeaf13c2197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-128421/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer-field/choices ["q-128421/selection/879a225aaf1b8272157c33247ace982b7e338d5701ba0d4d6c31dd38d4da6784" "q-128421/selection/a20b3c9808c291c56ec5bfc5f0f93a856fc692714ca7ebd36c5e4bc361f7075c" "q-128421/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-128421/selection/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" "q-128421/selection/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128421" :question/id #uuid "9c59800e-2701-5f60-8d3e-288359179eb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128421" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-128421/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe9711f6-e2ad-5eed-8ded-a6153b0322bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128421"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280722/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "bf549120-6114-5feb-b848-f01439d29d99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280722/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "45d1db52-a301-5925-a6a6-997e7f782f4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280722/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e414834f-173d-5fbb-bb6a-4f2a12084f4b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280722/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-280722/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" "q-280722/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280722" :question/id #uuid "875a18b4-72a0-591f-b9da-03167f35bd1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280722" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨1,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,2⟩$, and $c=⟨2,k,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\na\\cdot (b\\times c)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k & 5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ k & 5\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 5-2\\cdot k)-3(0\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 2)=(20-2k)+12 \\\\  & =32-2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 32-2k & =0 \\\\ -2k & =-32 \\\\ k & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280722/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280722"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-280720/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "bcdef9cd-da53-54f7-b9b4-1dc1d0848e2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-280720/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ddc02b8-3a95-5c91-b1c2-e5d366fdbe06" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-280720/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer-field/choices ["q-280720/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-280720" :question/id #uuid "d369a6bd-35ca-5c57-9419-5c24b72446a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-280720" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $x=⟨2,0,k⟩$, $y=⟨1,4,3⟩$, and $z=⟨0,2,5⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & k \\\\ 1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(4\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2)+0+k(1\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(20-6)+2k \\\\  & =28+2k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =0 \\\\ 28+2k & =0 \\\\ 2k & =-28 \\\\ k & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-14.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-280720/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-280720"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275353/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "13659ae6-e567-53cb-9aab-761952bceac9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275353/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "5b76fa60-842d-5b16-8204-99b6ff005fc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275353/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0cd9b70-e2f1-54e9-9ff7-5f2bc5f704cd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275353/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-275353/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-275353/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275353" :question/id #uuid "bd47ad71-726b-598c-9cd8-8f7ef7e44966" :question/math-academy-id "q-275353" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨-2,1,-3⟩$, $b=⟨-1,k,2⟩$, and $c=⟨3,-2,4⟩$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|+(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & k \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(k\\cdot 4-(-2)\\cdot 2)-((-1)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2)-3((-1)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-8k-8+10-6+9k \\\\  & =k-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ k-4 & =0 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275353/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275353"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048/selection/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" :answer/id #uuid "ec835b57-b746-5d80-9ba2-9c5230f8d1a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" :answer/id #uuid "1f8ea925-5c7c-5162-a7cb-d46308fa2426" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" :answer/id #uuid "506feec1-8f45-571f-9702-238851de28ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048/selection/85c8dd080b354b3b686d165fa5d6ef05632ba1519230ce6c65b5ecceb2c592a4" :answer/id #uuid "e1fda1c7-dbbf-5848-92c8-87c11f36f660" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae" :answer/id #uuid "add6a24a-4d07-5314-a478-1762592e98b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11449c7d-9008-5a04-b273-7f8f825ddaf4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42048/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" :answer-field/choices ["q-42048/selection/40a1a273986776af283f3fe5271d8cce9b3f9fa9c2c7fc5bf8516dd5a30de4b0" "q-42048/selection/a9d809426690fc6065e8673c85a555723d4ab72d745ec39834681473e579f93a" "q-42048/selection/ac9ae2052cc2e067abcad4ecf5a3f3d17a02fa2d9a881931a644b74ccc7546a6" "q-42048/selection/85c8dd080b354b3b686d165fa5d6ef05632ba1519230ce6c65b5ecceb2c592a4" "q-42048/selection/3c752b55a9d477bd0ba6387c5f2201a280295f1502439e3749cf69f3da3e0cae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42048" :question/id #uuid "258d49ee-e16c-5cac-8f15-2e4bb377a507" :question/math-academy-id "q-42048" :question/problem "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=⟨k,2,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,0,2⟩$ and $c=⟨4,1,3⟩$ are coplanar." :question/worked-solution "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)-2(3\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 2)+2(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-2k-2+6 \\\\  & =-2k+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ -2k+4 & =0 \\\\ 2k & =4 \\\\ k & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42048/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c84e5b-97a7-5116-a90c-e4f011e87cf0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "5a768aad-4442-5eeb-b551-844df002bec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "2e28d937-852d-5f0c-bb97-15536aedf7e5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" :answer/id #uuid "55b15b82-55b6-567a-b3c1-a2387a37ec7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "3df06724-6af5-531c-aec9-9679c50c5365" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "ed28cc46-223b-5dd5-8282-3e2fc22b7f49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1754209c-d9d5-5402-a2c6-523ddaed3744" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73746/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer-field/choices ["q-73746/selection/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" "q-73746/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-73746/selection/0fbe558572ecce67593db00d22f0d8d9d09c98d019451cd13488790a441e6c9c" "q-73746/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" "q-73746/selection/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73746" :question/id #uuid "0e77cbb8-c0a3-501c-a9ea-9b64ed425d73" :question/math-academy-id "q-73746" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(0,1,2)$, $B(-1,0,1)$, $C(1,1,0)$, and $D(3,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =i-2k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-2))-(1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =4+7+2 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|13|=13.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73746/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73746"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73753/selection/f