/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(-2,1,1)$, $B(2,1,0)$, $C(1,-1,2)$, and $D(3,-2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+j)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =4i-k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i-2j-2k)-(-2i+j+k) \\\\  & =5i-3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨5,-3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4((-2)\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot (-3))-0-(3\\cdot (-3)-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =36-1 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|35|=35.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73753/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "f8035a13-8cb2-5534-a42a-f98c2dc86b11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "57bc9b0e-3bab-5844-af84-e4c571c2be33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "8a92c1fc-1f6a-52c1-a15b-f8e954164b9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" :answer/id #uuid "0558ff42-1be5-5630-9918-2d6b027d7b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "804b614d-6206-5873-be9e-e700c6f4ef7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "52ff9321-5cc5-50d9-98cd-77b72128c0a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73744/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-73744/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-73744/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" "q-73744/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-73744/selection/e326a281f601aec64d5dcce4921033c5f93cbf7f8b0a7a5809a9962dfadde666" "q-73744/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73744" :question/id #uuid "287f03d9-5f5b-5d4e-a5e1-a25d62c26b2f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73744" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(1,1,0)$, $B(-2,1,0)$, $C(3,2,0)$, and $D(1,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =-3i \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =2i+1j \\\\  & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+3k)-(i+j) \\\\  & =3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0)-0+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-73744/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73744"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-281025/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "519fd9e0-4bf0-51e6-9a98-5ea8ab551b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-281025/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e5833afc-d2f4-5d52-b7a8-e6659db0c2c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-281025/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer-field/choices ["q-281025/field-1/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-281025" :question/id #uuid "0731c398-d5f2-578b-97ec-94db7b1c6288" :question/math-academy-id "q-281025" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,0,2),$ $B(5,1,3),$ $C(4,3,5),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5i+1j+3k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(3i+2k) \\\\  & =3k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(3\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)-1(1\\cdot 3-3\\cdot 0)+1(1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =2(9)-1(3)+1(0) \\\\  & =18-3+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-281025/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "57c790ad-c7fb-596c-8b60-cddd9b4e2165"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-281025"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
